1 INTRODUCTION
The term “avatar embodiment” describes the physical process that employs the Virtual Reality (VR) hardware and software to substitute (parts of) a person’s body with a virtual one [43]. Such a VR system captures the motion of a user’s body and uses it to animate a virtual character representing the self. This avatar is viewed in ﬁrst or third
